### Manual API tests — open in VS Code with the "REST Client" extension
### (by Huachao Mao), then click "Send Request" above each request.
### Start the API first: cd backend && npm run start:dev

@baseUrl = http://localhost:3000/api
@email = ana.test@example.com
@password = password123

### 1. Health check — should say status ok, db up
GET {{baseUrl}}/health

### 2. Register (run once; running it again gives 409 Conflict)
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{email}}",
  "password": "{{password}}"
}

### 3. Login — the token from this response is reused by every request below
# @name login
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{email}}",
  "password": "{{password}}"
}

### 4. Who am I?
@token = {{login.response.body.accessToken}}
GET {{baseUrl}}/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 5. Create a monitor — its id is captured below for steps 7–10
# @name created
POST {{baseUrl}}/monitors
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Example site",
  "url": "https://example.com",
  "intervalSeconds": 60
}

### 6. List my monitors
GET {{baseUrl}}/monitors
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 7. Get one monitor
@monitorId = {{created.response.body.id}}
GET {{baseUrl}}/monitors/{{monitorId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 7a. Dashboard overview (uptime + last 30 checks for every monitor)
GET {{baseUrl}}/monitors/overview
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 7b. Stats for one monitor
GET {{baseUrl}}/monitors/{{monitorId}}/stats
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 7c. Response-time history (24h | 7d | 30d)
GET {{baseUrl}}/monitors/{{monitorId}}/history?range=24h
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 7d. Incidents
GET {{baseUrl}}/monitors/{{monitorId}}/incidents
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 7e. Show it on the public status page
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/monitors/{{monitorId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "isPublic": true }

### 7f. My status page link
# @name statusPage
GET {{baseUrl}}/status-page
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 7g. The public page — no token needed
GET {{baseUrl}}/public/status/{{statusPage.response.body.slug}}

### 8. Pause it
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/monitors/{{monitorId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "isActive": false
}

### 9. Resume it and switch to GET
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/monitors/{{monitorId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "isActive": true,
  "method": "GET"
}

### 10. Delete it (204 No Content), then step 7's GET (rerun it) gives 404
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/monitors/{{monitorId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}


### ===== Things that SHOULD fail =====

### 11. SSRF: EC2 metadata address → 400
POST {{baseUrl}}/monitors
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "evil", "url": "http://169.254.169.254/latest/meta-data/" }

### 12. SSRF: our own machine → 400
POST {{baseUrl}}/monitors
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "evil", "url": "http://localhost:5432" }

### 13. SSRF: a Docker container name → 400
POST {{baseUrl}}/monitors
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "evil", "url": "http://db:5432" }

### 14. SSRF: 127.0.0.1 disguised as a decimal number → 400
POST {{baseUrl}}/monitors
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "evil", "url": "http://2130706433" }

### 15. Interval below 60 seconds → 400
POST {{baseUrl}}/monitors
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "too fast", "url": "https://example.org", "intervalSeconds": 10 }

### 16. Trying to set someone else's userId → 400 (unknown field rejected)
POST {{baseUrl}}/monitors
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "sneaky", "url": "https://example.org", "userId": "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000" }

### 17. Domain that doesn't exist → 400
POST {{baseUrl}}/monitors
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "nope", "url": "https://this-domain-does-not-exist-12345.com" }

### 18. No token → 401
GET {{baseUrl}}/monitors

### 19. Wrong password → 401 (same message as an unknown email)
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "{{email}}", "password": "wrong-password" }
